
The Router does not directly understand or interact with
Custom Resources. Something has to translate that information
into configuraton and commands that it does understand.

That's the Adaptor.

ontroller decides what should exist, then the Adaptor expresses
that in language that the Router can consume.

It also sets up the links to other Routers.

But information also goes the other way.
It is only the Router that knows the actual state of things like 
links. So the Adaptor gets information from it -- maybe using
info from Vanflow -- and then informs the Controller, which then
updates the current status of the relevant Custom Resources.
